Ported models
-------------

Metascape includes models ported from Ascape 5.6.1 and from the Eclipse
Agent Modeling Platform. Every ported file names, in its header, the legacy
classes or model file it was ported from and keeps the original copyright
line. Each model also carries its provenance (authors, publication, source
and copyright), which Metascape Studio shows next to the model, and each
model family's README lists every legacy class and how it was ported.

packages/models/src/brookings/
  The Brookings Institution models (Sugarscape, Artificial Anasazi, Civil
  Violence, Norms, Retirement, Emergence of Classes, Emergence of Firms,
  Demographic Prisoner's Dilemma, Diffusion, Conway's Life, Busy Beavers,
  the Coordination Game tutorial and Simple), ported from the edu.brook
  packages of Ascape, and the Spatial Iterated Prisoner's Dilemma, ported
  from name.milesparker.spatialipd.
    Copyright 1998-2007 The Brookings Institution, with revisions by
    Metascape LLC, and others (spatial IPD: Copyright 2000 Miles T. Parker).
    BSD license: LICENSES/brookings-models-license.txt

packages/models/src/ascape/
  The Ascape example models (Bionland, Boids, Traffic), ported from
  org.ascape.examples.
packages/engine/src/space/grid/small-world.ts
  Follows the neighbor rule of org.ascape.model.space.Array2DSmallWorld.
    Copyright 1998-2007 The Brookings Institution, NuTech Solutions, Inc.,
    Metascape LLC, and contributors.
    BSD license: LICENSES/ascape-license.txt

These files are distributed under EPL-2.0 for the port and under the BSD
license above for the original work (SPDX: EPL-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause).

packages/models/src/amp/
  The Eclipse Agent Modeling Platform example models (StupidModel, Wiki
  Example, Heatbugs, Demographic Prisoner's Dilemma, Epidemic, Markets and
  SIR), ported from their .metaabm model files. These were made available
  under the Eclipse Public License and are distributed under EPL-2.0.

The Heatbugs model in Ascape's edu.brooksantafe package was not ported: that
directory carries a GNU GPL notice.
